{
  "info": {
    "name": "AAFM Dashboard API (Tier 1)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Multi-tenant analytics dashboard API: Org → Team hierarchy, RLS isolation, server-side sessions.\n\n**Setup**\n1. `npm run migrate && npm run seed && npm run dev` in `backend/`.\n2. The suite signs in ~11 times; the default auth rate limit is 10 per 15 min per IP, so set `AUTH_RATE_LIMIT=100` in `backend/.env` for local runs.\n3. Run the whole collection in order with the Collection Runner (folders build on each other's saved variables).\n\n**How auth works here**: the session is an HttpOnly cookie that Postman's cookie jar keeps automatically. Each `Sign in` request switches the active user. Every write sends `X-Requested-With` (CSRF guard); requests in `07 Security` omit it on purpose.\n\nSeed users (org `acme`, password `Password@123`): super@ (Super Admin), alice@ (Finance admin + Marketing viewer), bob@ (Finance editor), carol@ (Marketing viewer), dave@ (Marketing admin)."
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000"
    },
    {
      "key": "org",
      "value": "acme"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "Password@123"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 Health",
      "description": "Liveness and database readiness. No auth.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/health"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Ready (DB ping)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/ready"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
